From: Stained Glass OS <ke7oxh@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] server: sandboxes read what SYSTEM re-created in HKLM (Chrome had no sound)

The token default DACL of the shared prefix (0002/0248) grants "users read" to this machine's
Domain Users (S-1-5-21-0-0-0-513, the primary group), plus RESTRICTED and ALL APPLICATION PACKAGES.
Every key SYSTEM creates, or re-creates while it has no descriptor (HKLM\Software\Classes at every
boot), gets that DACL. A sandbox's restricted token keeps only Everyone, BUILTIN\Users,
Interactive, Authenticated Users, the logon SID and the user enabled and makes every other group
deny-only, so its normal access check found no grant: Chrome's audio service (USER_LIMITED, low
integrity) could not open HKLM\Software\Classes, CoCreateInstance(MMDeviceEnumerator) failed ("no
class object ... could be created"), Chrome used its fake audio output and the Windows build of
Chrome had no sound at all. --disable-features=AudioServiceSandbox made it play.

The default DACL now also grants BUILTIN\Users read, as Windows' HKLM does. The display keys' DACL
(which shares the helper) gains the same read ACE; nothing gains write.

Verified on qa3 (release 659 + this server): HKLM\Software\Classes is
...(A;;GR;;;S-1-5-21-0-0-0-513)(A;;GR;;;BU)(A;;GR;;;RC)(A;;GR;;;AC); Chrome's sandboxed audio
service (--service-sandbox-type=audio) opens a PipeWire stream ("Google Chrome" sink input, sink
RUNNING). Mutant SG_MUTANT_NO_BUILTIN_USERS_READ builds the old DACL (10.0-874: no sink input).
---
diff --git a/server/token.c b/server/token.c
--- a/server/token.c
+++ b/server/token.c
@@ -1307,13 +1307,31 @@
  * nothing in HKLM -- not even the display configuration -- and could not make
  * a window. */
 static const struct sid restricted_code_sid = { SID_REVISION, 1, SECURITY_NT_AUTHORITY, { SECURITY_RESTRICTED_CODE_RID } };
+/* Stained Glass OS: and BUILTIN\Users, which is whom Windows' HKLM grants read. The "users read"
+ * ACE below names this machine's Domain Users (the primary group), but a sandbox's restricted
+ * token keeps only Everyone, Users, Interactive, Authenticated Users, the logon SID and the user
+ * enabled and makes every other group deny-only. Chrome's audio service (USER_LIMITED, low
+ * integrity) then could not open HKLM\Software\Classes -- re-created by SYSTEM at boot, so it
+ * carries this DACL -- CoCreateInstance(MMDeviceEnumerator) failed and Chrome played every sound
+ * into its fake output: no sound at all (2026-11-13). */
+#ifndef SG_MUTANT_NO_BUILTIN_USERS_READ
+#define SG_SANDBOX_READ_ACES 3
+#else
 #define SG_SANDBOX_READ_ACES 2
+#endif
 static struct ace *sg_add_sandbox_read( struct ace *ace )
 {
+#ifndef SG_MUTANT_NO_BUILTIN_USERS_READ
+    ace = set_ace( ace_next( ace ), &builtin_users_sid, ACCESS_ALLOWED_ACE_TYPE, 0, GENERIC_READ );
+#endif
     ace = set_ace( ace_next( ace ), &restricted_code_sid, ACCESS_ALLOWED_ACE_TYPE, 0, GENERIC_READ );
     return set_ace( ace_next( ace ), &all_app_packages_sid, ACCESS_ALLOWED_ACE_TYPE, 0, GENERIC_READ );
 }
+#ifndef SG_MUTANT_NO_BUILTIN_USERS_READ
+#define SG_SANDBOX_READ_SIZE (SG_SANDBOX_READ_ACES * sizeof(struct ace) + sid_len( &builtin_users_sid ) + sid_len( &restricted_code_sid ) + sid_len( &all_app_packages_sid ))
+#else
 #define SG_SANDBOX_READ_SIZE (SG_SANDBOX_READ_ACES * sizeof(struct ace) + sid_len( &restricted_code_sid ) + sid_len( &all_app_packages_sid ))
+#endif
 
 static struct acl *sg_create_system_dacl( const struct sid *user_sid )
 {
